  <h2 id="what-is-cet">What MHT-CET actually is, and why "CET" and "NEET" keep getting mixed up</h2>

  <p>
    MHT-CET is the Maharashtra Health and Technical Common Entrance Test, run every year by the State Common Entrance Test Cell, a body under the Government of Maharashtra.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most students and families just call it "CET." That shorthand is where the confusion starts.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">What CET is not</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>It is not a national exam. It is a Maharashtra state exam, run by a state body, mainly serving Maharashtra colleges.</li>
      <li>It is not the same exam as NEET, even though both PCB students sit a biology-heavy paper.</li>
      <li>It is not one single exam covering every health and science course — nursing runs on its own separate CET.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      Get this distinction right before you plan your whole year around it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    For PCB students specifically, MHT-CET runs a dedicated PCB-group paper alongside the PCM-group paper used for engineering.
  </p>

  <p>
    That PCB paper is the actual gateway this article is about.
  </p>

