  <p>
    The paper totals 200 marks, runs as a computer-based test, and gives you 180 minutes.
  </p>

  <p>
    There is no negative marking, and roughly 20% of questions draw from the Class 11 syllabus with the remaining 80% from Class 12.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    Exam dates move every year — the PCB group typically runs in April, after the PCM group. Check the current schedule on the official CET Cell site before planning your board-exam-to-CET timeline.
  </p>

